.TH MYGREP 1 "September 2026" "OS Assignment 01" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for matching lines

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The mygrep function searches the lines of a file for a specified string. Matching lines are stored in a dynamically allocated array. The function returns the number of matching lines or -1 when an error occurs.

